<Alert Color="Color.Warning" Visible>
    <AlertDescription>
        <Strong>Never use a License Key as the value of <Code>ProductToken</Code> or place a License Key in application code, configuration, deployment files, or client-side assets.</Strong>
    </AlertDescription>
</Alert>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    See <Anchor To="docs/usage/licensing/register-product-token#protecting-your-producttoken" Title="Protecting your ProductToken">Protecting your ProductToken</Anchor> for storage, local development, production, CI/CD, and Blazor WebAssembly guidance.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    License behavior
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    A valid commercial ProductToken removes licensing warnings and licensed component limits. A Community ProductToken applies the Community license and displays a compact <Strong>Community License</Strong> button in the bottom-right corner. Select the button to open the full license notice.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    A missing or invalid ProductToken is treated as unlicensed and displays the applicable warning and component limits. An expired token displays the applicable expired-license notice.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Get a ProductToken
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Follow the <Anchor To="docs/usage/licensing/register-product-token" Title="Configure a ProductToken">ProductToken configuration guide</Anchor> to get a ProductToken from your Blazorise account and configure your application.
</DocsPageParagraph>